        "text": "`pipe` accepts an initial value followed by callables and returns the result of applying those callables from left to right."
      },
      {
        "id": "B003",
        "text": "`curry` wraps a callable so that required positional arguments may be supplied across successive calls or together in one call."
      },
      {
        "id": "B004",
        "text": "A curried callable accepts keyword arguments, preserves defaulted parameters, and combines them with positional arguments supplied by a later call."
      },
